WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.500
One asset. One continuous workflow.
Fusion Studio 0.19.0-rc.1 · fresh workspace · normal playback speed

2
00:00:02.500 --> 00:00:16.733
01 / Import a DAZ asset
Open SPowered Trunk.duf and review conversion limits before importing.

3
00:00:16.733 --> 00:00:39.367
02 / Inspect the editable scene
Frame the imported asset, orbit around it, then inspect its topology.

4
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:46.867
03 / Make a precise edit
Select the imported root and set its Y rotation to 25 degrees.

5
00:00:46.867 --> 00:00:55.133
04 / Undo, then redo
Recover the original transform, then restore the edit through scene history.

6
00:00:55.133 --> 00:01:04.000
05 / Save a project version
Name the project Trunk Study and save its editable scene.

7
00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.667
06 / Reopen the saved project
Open the saved .fusion file; geometry and transforms restore from disk.

8
00:01:10.667 --> 00:01:21.700
07 / Export a validated GLB
Create a new interchange file; inspect the actual glTF validation result.

9
00:01:21.700 --> 00:01:27.733
08 / Light the scene
Add a three-point lighting rig and save the lit scene before rendering.

10
00:01:27.733 --> 00:03:56.933
09 / Render the result
Cycles · OptiX · 1920 × 1080 · 32 samples. Render wait retained.

11
00:03:56.933 --> 00:04:03.633
Workflow complete.
Imported → inspected → edited → recovered → saved → reopened → exported → rendered.
